	spec: 'Every effective session model change, including /model, picker selections, /intro and intro completion, reports a readable switch from the previous model to the new model, with available display names and actual provider/model IDs and effort suffixes. The shared change path owns formatting, user output and durable model delivery. During active work, the switch fact precedes the continuation instruction in one notice; cwd-only changes retain safe continuation. Both web and terminal use shared output without duplicate notice cards. Model-run commands retain their tool-result attribution. Unchanged or invalid selections create no switch notice. Preserve effort normalization, warnings, current display names, bare /model status and safe handoff including pauses and unsafe tools. Prefer fewer source lines without sacrificing readability or behavior. This replaces task 71z model-output suppression; its /config requirements remain. Invariant: every effective model change is explicitly visible to user and model, regardless of entry point.',
