		'Refactor supersedes the original command-local implementation: slash.change owns switch formatting, attributed UI output and durable notices for every caller. It formats from known base IDs plus qualified IDs, never splitting colons. One model-name event supplies both formatting and client metadata. Active switches append continuation instructions to the switch fact before steering; idle or already-aborted work gets the switch fact only. COMMAND acknowledgements reuse the returned text without a duplicate visible card, and unchanged selections retain their done acknowledgement. Current Hal display names and bare /model status remain unchanged. The refactor removes one non-test source line overall; extended existing contract tests add eight lines. One combined history notice replaces two on active /model changes, with no polling or growing auxiliary state. Verification: 58 focused tests across ten files passed; tsc --noEmit and changed-file oxlint passed. Unsafe work can defer interruption across successive changes, so each change may legitimately carry continuation instructions.'
